From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: WindowsReplaceString, HSTRING_User*, CoWaitForMultipleObjects and two COM calls

Exported stubs in combase that a program importing them could not use:
WindowsReplaceString (every occurrence of a string replaced, left to right,
without overlap; a NULL replacement deletes; an empty result is NULL),
HSTRING_UserSize/Marshal/Unmarshal/Free and their 64-bit names (an HSTRING
sent between apartments: a ULONG length and the characters, a NULL string a
zero length), CoWaitForMultipleObjects (the same wait as
CoWaitForMultipleHandles), CoInvalidateRemoteMachineBindings and
CoAllowUnmarshalerCLSID.

---
--- a/dlls/combase/combase.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/combase.c
@@ -3695,3 +3695,29 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DllGetClassObject(REFCLSID rclsid, REFIID riid, void **obj)
 
     return CLASS_E_CLASSNOTAVAILABLE;
 }
+
+
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           CoInvalidateRemoteMachineBindings    (combase.@)
+ *
+ * Drops cached binding handles to a machine; none are cached here.
+ */
+HRESULT WINAPI CoInvalidateRemoteMachineBindings(LPOLESTR server)
+{
+    TRACE("%s\n", debugstr_w(server));
+
+    return S_OK;
+}
+
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           CoAllowUnmarshalerCLSID    (combase.@)
+ *
+ * Adds a class to the list of those allowed to unmarshal; every class is
+ * allowed to here.
+ */
+HRESULT WINAPI CoAllowUnmarshalerCLSID(REFCLSID clsid)
+{
+    TRACE("%s\n", debugstr_guid(clsid));
+
+    return clsid ? S_OK : E_INVALIDARG;
+}
